# ============================================
# Issue: zeabur-kube-watch CrashLoopBackOff
# Captured: 2026-06-07 (during troubleshooting)
# Source: kubectl logs n/zeabur-kube-watch --tail=50
# Severity: error
# ============================================
# Symptom: kube-watch pod keeps restarting because it can't reach
# the NATS server. DNS resolution for `nats.zeabur.com` fails because
# CoreDNS doesn't have a rewrite rule and the external name is unreachable
# from WSL2 (no route to internet for *.zeabur.com on port 4222 directly).

2026/06/07 14:23:01 kube-watch starting up
2026/06/07 14:23:01 Loading config from /etc/kube-watch/config.yaml
2026/06/07 14:23:01 Region: server-6a23cdf424701a8493345c17
2026/06/07 14:23:01 Vector URL: http://vector-aggregator:8081/k8s-events
2026/06/07 14:23:01 NATS URL: nats://zeabur-kube-watch:<REDACTED>@nats.zeabur.com:4222
2026/06/07 14:23:01 Connecting to NATS at nats.zeabur.com:4222...
2026/06/07 14:23:31 dial tcp: lookup nats.zeabur.com on 10.43.0.10:53: no such host
2026/06/07 14:23:31 Failed to connect: timeout waiting for NATS
2026/06/07 14:23:31 Retrying in 5s...
2026/06/07 14:23:36 Connecting to NATS at nats.zeabur.com:4222...
2026/06/07 14:24:06 dial tcp: lookup nats.zeabur.com on 10.43.0.10:53: no such host
2026/06/07 14:24:06 Failed to connect: timeout waiting for NATS
2026/06/07 14:24:06 Retrying in 5s...
2026/06/07 14:24:11 Connecting to NATS at nats.zeabur.com:4222...
2026/06/07 14:24:41 dial tcp: lookup nats.zeabur.com on 10.43.0.10:53: no such host
2026/06/07 14:24:41 FATAL: cannot start without NATS connection
2026/06/07 14:24:41 exiting

# ============================================
# Analysis
# ============================================
# - The kube-watch binary hardcodes `nats.zeabur.com` as the NATS host
# - It ignores NATS_URL, NATS_USER, NATS_PASSWORD env vars
# - CoreDNS has no rewrite rule for nats.zeabur.com
# - DNS query times out because external nats.zeabur.com is unreachable
#
# Fix options:
#   1. Add CoreDNS rewrite: nats.zeabur.com -> nats.default.svc.cluster.local
#   2. Disable NATS auth (so the hardcoded credentials work)
#   Both required.
